{"entity": "Chalcogenide Glass", "type": "naturalobject", "description": "Chalcogenide glass is a class of amorphous glass materials that serves as the foundational material for phase change memory (PCM/PRAM) technology. Its defining property is the ability to undergo reversible phase transitions between amorphous (glassy) and crystalline states. These transitions constitute the physical basis of phase change memory: data is stored by switching the material between these two structural phases, and device operation exploits the distinct intermediate resistance states associated with the material's phase configuration. In this capacity, chalcogenide glass functions as the storage medium of PCM devices.

