{"entity1": "Chalcogenide Materials", "entity2": "Ge2Sb2Te5", "description": "The relation between Chalcogenide Materials and Ge2Sb2Te5 establishes Ge2Sb2Te5 as a specific example of the chalcogenide material class. Also referred to by its abbreviation GST, Ge2Sb2Te5 is a chalcogenide alloy that is frequently cited in the literature as a representative member of this family of materials. As an alloy, it exemplifies the composition-based nature of chalcogenide materials, which are compounds formed from chalcogen elements combined with other elements such as germanium and antimony.

Ge2Sb2Te5 is particularly significant for its role in phase-change memory technology. It is widely recognized as the typical chalcogenide material used in this application, and it is consistently cited as an example of a chalcogenide material employed in phase-change memory devices. Its relevance extends to the broader category of Phase-Change Materials, where it serves as a specific material type enabling non-volatile data storage through reversible structural transitions.

The functional properties of Ge2Sb2Te5 underpin its technological importance. As a chalcogenide alloy, it exhibits switching effects and phase-change transitions, allowing it to reversibly shift between different structural states. Additionally, Ge2Sb2Te5 alloys display different optical reflectivity between their phases, a characteristic that enables the distinction and readout of the material's states. Together, these attributes—reversible switching, phase-change behavior, and phase-dependent optical reflectivity—make Ge2Sb2Te5 a canonical example of chalcogenide materials and a cornerstone material for phase-change memory applications."}
